  <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 24px;">STOP - Read the Following:</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 16px;">Congratulations!!</p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px;">Your software token has been assigned. You will need to complete the following steps in order to use RSA SecurID with Pulse Secure.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 18px;">Step 1: RSA SecurID Client Application Download</h3>
    <p style="font-size: 14px;">The RSA SecurID Client application must be downloaded an installed on your system. Your operating system must be checked for <span data-field="os_version_check">{{ os_version_check }}</span> prior to implementation. Follow the instructions in the slides provided to accomplish this task. You will need to have a <span data-field="system_administrator_role">{{ system_administrator_role }}</span> on site when completing the installation for elevated rights. <a href="#" style="color: blue;">Please view all slides prior to executing instructions.</a></p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 18px;">Step 2: Import Soft Token for RSA SecurID Client</h3>
    <p style="font-size: 14px;">This section will guide you through the process of importing your soft token, from the ZIP file (<span data-field="zip_file_name">{{ zip_file_name }}</span>) provided to you by the RSA system administrator, sent to you by email. Please follow the instructions provided in the slides to accomplish the import. <a href="#" style="color: blue;">Please view all slides prior to executing instructions.</a></p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 18px;">Step 3: Create Your Software Token PIN</h3>
    <p style="font-size: 14px;">To set your PIN, go to the VSU RSA Self-Service Console (<a href="#" style="color: blue;">https://rsaveb.vsu.edu</a>) and login with your Active Directory username (standard user, not elevated). When prompted for Authentication method, select "Password". Depending on the browser you are using, you may see a notice that "There is a problem with this website's security certificate" or "Your connection is not secure". In this case, select the 'Continue to this website' or 'Advanced' option. If prompted, add an exception for the site's security certificate. Next, use the link to 'Create PIN' or 'Change PIN'. Set a 4-8 digit PIN. You will receive confirmation that your PIN has been set successfully.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 18px;">Step 4: Test PIN and RSA SecurID Client Soft Token</h3>
    <p style="font-size: 14px;">Next return to the Self-Service Console and then select 'test' link. To test your token, enter your username in the 'User ID' field. In the 'Password' field, first type your <span data-field="pin_value">{{ pin_value }}</span> followed by the 6-digit code displayed in the Tokencode screen of the RSA SecurID Client application (for example, if your PIN is 1234 and your Tokencode displays 753164, your Password would be '1234753164'). Next, click the Test button. You should see a success screen. If the test fails, wait for the next token code and try again. If the test still fails, please contact the system administrator.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 18px;">Step 5: Pulse Secure VPN Configuration</h3>
    <p style="font-size: 14px;">To use your token to authenticate to the Pulse Secure VPN, you will need to 'add' a new connection entry in the Pulse Secure Client. The 'Name' will be <span data-field="vpn_name">{{ vpn_name }}</span> and the 'Server URL' for the new connection should be: <a href="#" style="color: blue;">https://secure.vsu.edu/securid-rsa</a></p>
  </div>
</div>

